const contentHtml = `<p class="lead">Most local SEO checklists fail home service businesses. They assume you have a storefront, a fixed address customers visit, and a simple service menu. They ignore the reality of service-area businesses — plumbers who drive 40 miles for emergency calls, HVAC technicians covering three counties, roofers who never see a customer walk through a door.</p>
<p>This checklist was built for you. Every one of the 50 items addresses the specific challenges contractors face: competing in the Google Local Pack without a visible address, generating reviews from one-time customers, building citations when you serve 15 cities, and creating location pages that Google trusts rather than penalizes as "doorway pages."</p>
<p>Here is the reality: 46% of all Google searches have local intent (Google, 2018). Businesses in the Local Pack receive 126% more traffic than those ranking only in organic results (BrightLocal, 2025). Yet 56% of businesses have not claimed their Google Business Profile, and only 44% of claimed profiles are fully optimized (SearchLab, 2026). The opportunity is massive. The competition is weaker than you think.</p>
<p>This checklist covers 7 categories: Google Business Profile, Reviews, Website, Citations, Content, Technical SEO, and Advanced Strategies. Each item includes a priority rating (Must-Have, Important, or Advanced), a 50-word explanation of why it matters, a 100-word implementation guide, a time estimate, and the tool or resource needed.</p>
<p>Work through Must-Have items first. They deliver the fastest ranking improvements. Important items build the foundation for sustained visibility. Advanced items separate market leaders from the pack.</p>
