<h2>Key Takeaways</h2>
<ul>
<li>Google Business Profile optimization accounts for 36% of local pack ranking factors — it is your highest-ROI local SEO activity.</li>
<li>Review velocity matters more than total count. Generate 5-10 new Google reviews monthly and respond to all reviews within 48 hours.</li>
<li>NAP consistency across every platform is non-negotiable. Even minor variations split your ranking authority.</li>
<li>Location pages need genuinely unique content — copy-paste city swaps trigger Google penalties.</li>
<li>Local SEO is an ongoing system, not a one-time project. Quarterly audits catch decay before it impacts revenue.</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Conclusion</h2>
<p>Local SEO is the highest-leverage marketing channel for home service businesses. 46% of Google searches have local intent. 76% of local mobile searchers visit a business within 24 hours. 28% of those visits result in a purchase. The data is clear: local searchers are actively looking to hire contractors right now.</p>
<p>The businesses that win are not the ones with the biggest budgets. They are the ones that execute consistently on the fundamentals: a fully optimized GBP, systematic review generation, consistent citations, fast mobile websites, and locally relevant content.</p>
<p>This checklist gives you the exact 50 items to complete, in priority order, with time estimates and tool recommendations. Start with Must-Have items this week. Build momentum. Track results. Your competitors are not doing this work — which means every item you complete is a competitive advantage.</p>
<p>The 30-day action plan above is your starting point. Print it. Assign tasks. Check items off as you complete them. In 90 days, you will have a local SEO foundation that generates leads for years.</p>
